From dfaebe5eddaea225a247334f3e56212bf476f69c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Semih Baskan <strst.gs@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:16:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: BCM5301X: RT-N18U: use the flow accelerator

Use the prepended Broadcom tag on port 8, the CPU port, so that the
flow accelerator in front of it is in the path. Describe port 5 (gmac0)
as a second CPU port with a fixed link for the switch's trap rules (TTL
0 and 1, TCP FIN and RST). A switch tree has one tagger, so port 5
names brcm-prepend too, which uses the regular tag on that port. The
two ports follow the EA6900 patches of the flow accelerator series.
This RT-N18U's switch reports revision 5 at boot ("found switch:
BCM53011, rev 5"), which has the accelerator.

Measured on an RT-N18U: one TCP stream from the LAN to a host behind the
WAN port runs through the accelerator at 948 Mbit/s, and at 949 Mbit/s
the other way.

Signed-off-by: Semih Baskan <strst.gs@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm47081-asus-rt-n18u.dts | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm47081-asus-rt-n18u.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm47081-asus-rt-n18u.dts
@@ -134,11 +134,20 @@
 		};
 
 		port@5 {
-			status = "disabled";
+			dsa-tag-protocol = "brcm-prepend";
+
+			fixed-link {
+				speed = <1000>;
+				full-duplex;
+			};
 		};
 
 		port@7 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
+
+		port@8 {
+			dsa-tag-protocol = "brcm-prepend";
+		};
 	};
 };
